task: intent-slot-extraction
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-04
branch: feature/intent-slot-extraction
worktree: ../okay-wt-extract

why: The operator asked for the end-to-end extractors, and they are
  the hole between the classifier and the act: a frame can only be
  ASKED, never FILLED FROM THE MESSAGE IT CAME WITH. "Are you free
  Wednesday afternoon?" is classified, and then the router asks "When
  would you like to meet?" of someone who just said. `Temporal.parse`
  already scans a whole word list, so the machinery exists and is
  simply not wired to a slot.

what: a `Slot` may carry an extractor; `Frame.fillFrom(message, lang)`
  runs the unanswered ones over the message and keeps the EVIDENCE
  span beside the value; the router fills before it asks.

note: intent-taxon-wired-to-tiers was claimed and released unstarted —
  no code was written — because the operator's ask takes the lane.
  It stays in BACKLOG.md, unclaimed and available.

files: okay-intent/src/main/scala/okay/intent/{Slot,Temporal}.scala,
  okay-intent tests, okay-demo/IntentRouter.scala,
  specs/intent-classify.md, BACKLOG.md
